  "visualBrief": "The Málaga Cathedral exterior centers on three recessed west portals, the completed pediment and the stepped plaza entrance. The domed north bell tower rises above the unfinished south tower. The east apse and aisle buttresses frame the dark nave roof underlay and exposed timber trusses seen in November 2026.",
  "heightPolicy": "The 22 m sea-level datum follows standard viewer terrain. The foundations extend below the terrain, the main stair rises from the mapped plaza, and the north tower rises 87 m above its sampled footing.",
  "nativeAxes": "Positive X runs from the west entry at Plaza del Obispo toward the apse. Positive Z points toward the unfinished south tower.",
  "limitations": [
    "The exterior depicts the durable fabric visible in November 2026, including the completed west pediment, the timber apse roof framing and the dark protection on the nave. Roof coverage is approximate while the work is ongoing.",
    "The scaffold, cranes and eventual finished roof are outside this dated exterior model. Decorative figures, heraldry and clock detail are represented at viewing scale.",
    "The cathedral footprint and west facing derive from PMTiles. The bell tower height follows the cathedral chapter’s 87 m figure. Other heights are exterior estimates on standard viewer terrain."
  ],
